From 4c7fdf024c6898d8f792b004e46ff1080b210d60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:44:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: HDR10+, the metadata of each frame in the
 commit of that frame

The HDR10+ InfoFrame of a picture (VideoPicture::hdr10PlusVsif) now goes out
with the frame that shows it, through one path for every driver: a driver
that can send it next to the HDR InfoFrame, and change it with a flip and
never with a change of mode, gives its connectors HDR10PLUS_VSIF, a blob of
the 27 bytes of its payload. The Hades kernel patches give it to nvidia-drm,
amdgpu, i915 and xe.

The renderers (GLES, DRM PRIME on GLES and on a plane) hand the window
system the payload of the picture they draw, for each frame of a video
whose HDR they pass through as it is (not a picture rebuilt from Dolby
Vision, nor native Dolby Vision). CWinSystemGbm::SetHDR10Plus() queues it
in the request of that frame's flip, so it never adds a commit or changes
the cadence, and only while:
- the HDR of the video is signalled as PQ (HDR10: HDR10+ is HDR10 and its
  metadata), which CHDRSignal keeps true to what is queued;
- the display declares HDR10+ (its HDR10+ vendor-specific video data block,
  application version 1 or later, read by DisplayInfo);
- the connector has HDR10PLUS_VSIF.
Otherwise, and for a frame without HDR10+ metadata, what was queued is taken
away and the output is plain HDR10, as without this; the HDR InfoFrame is
never touched. The same payload is not queued twice, and the blobs of the
last ones are kept while a request that falls back may still name them.

A driver that does not take it: the commits that carried it fall back to the
request before, so what the kernel keeps for HDR10PLUS_VSIF is never a value
that was queued. After eight such commits HDR10+ stops for the video and
the log says so; the next video tries again. Each case is written to the
log once per video. The decisions are in HDR10PlusOutput.h, which a host
test runs; HDR10+ is reported as a capability of the display only where it
can go out.
